00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:47.100
We are thinking about.

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:50.600
We're working in India with
things like Read Along.

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:51.640
There's a lot of different things

00:16:51.640 --> 00:16:52.930
that are needed in different contexts.

00:16:52.930 --> 00:16:55.710
And we are thinking about those...

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:58.840
That range of needs and what we can build

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:01.830
that will satisfy broad
needs around the world,

00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:03.170
but also specialized needs

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:05.333
in particular places that arise.

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:07.493
- Yeah.

00:17:08.490 --> 00:17:10.490
That different context is so important.

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:13.220
They mentioned the importance
of tests and quizzes,

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:16.140
and that is something
that is quite different

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:18.120
in different education systems.

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:20.696
And how they think summative tests

00:17:20.696 --> 00:17:23.740
and even things like
the size of classrooms

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:25.140
can make a difference.

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:26.260
It seems like...

00:17:27.430 --> 00:17:31.000
How do you think about
kind of just assembling...

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:32.490
Speaking of information,

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:35.060
assembling all of that
information together.

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:37.130
So it kind of get your, you know,

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:39.033
build your knowledge base there.

00:17:40.837 --> 00:17:42.230
- I think, I mean,

00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:43.530
I'm acutely aware of the difference

00:17:43.530 --> 00:17:46.730
having come from a different
educational system myself.

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:47.663
And so,

00:17:48.690 --> 00:17:49.523
I think that

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:52.160
in many ways we are looking at

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:54.680
education in various countries.

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:58.500
There are some of the countries
like Brazil, Indonesia,

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:01.530
India, to get a sense of what is happening

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:02.363
in different places,

00:18:02.363 --> 00:18:04.350
what the needs are in different places.

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:07.810
In many places the way education works

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:10.210
is driven by sort of the government...

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:12.660
By policy, by government policy.

00:18:12.660 --> 00:18:13.680
And so we need to understand

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:15.740
what's happening in these
different countries,

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:17.490
on a country by country basis.

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:19.683
And so we are looking
at it in those terms.

00:18:20.650 --> 00:18:22.000
- Got it. That makes sense.

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:26.310
So here's again, a bit
of a different question.

00:18:26.310 --> 00:18:27.850
But I think I'd be interested to hear

00:18:27.850 --> 00:18:29.170
what you have to say from...

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:32.610
Let me see, who is asking
Jennifer Zhao on Facebook.

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:34.270
What do you think are key skills

00:18:34.270 --> 00:18:36.720
students should learn to
be ready for the future?

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:42.460
- You know at the end of
the day, (exhales sharply)

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:44.300
the future is going to be...

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:49.040
Changes faster and faster and faster pace.

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:50.430
So one of the key skills

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:53.610
I think is getting
comfortable with learning.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:56.047
Which is why I come back to
that notion of curiosity,

00:18:56.047 --> 00:18:58.110
because that's what makes learning fun.

00:18:58.110 --> 00:18:59.690
Because if it's self driven

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:01.610
and it's driven by curiosity,
it makes learning fun.

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:03.930
But that also enables you

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:07.120
to like keep continue to learn over time.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:10.120
And so I think the key skill ends up being

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:12.373
a little bit meta in my view.

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:17.083
It is that ability to continue to learn.

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:20.860
And to some extent on the particulars

00:19:20.860 --> 00:19:22.100
continue to be important.

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:24.320
Language is gonna continue
to be important mathematics

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:27.880
and the sciences and so on
and continue to be important.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:29.990
But as foundational.

00:19:29.990 --> 00:19:32.890
But beyond that I think
there are different skills

00:19:32.890 --> 00:19:35.440
that we'll need at over time

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.790
that are gonna be hard
to predict right now.

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:42.120
And so being flexible and
adaptable to that future,

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:45.090
I think is gonna be really
important for people

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:47.943
to not just survive, but
thrive in that future.

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:55.170
- So another concern
about the future is equity

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:58.310
and leveling the playing fields.

00:19:58.310 --> 00:20:00.633
Is there a role for technology there?

00:20:01.981 --> 00:20:03.370
- You know, there are lots of ways

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:04.550
in which we're thinking about this.

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:05.520
Like one example

00:20:07.360 --> 00:20:08.890
is how do we...

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:10.270
Is during COVID.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:13.110
Like a lot of places don't
have access to the internet.

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:14.940
They don't have WiFi access

00:20:16.439 --> 00:20:19.660
or high-speed or phone access.

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:22.650
And so we have been working
on making much more of us

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:25.870
of our apps be available offline.

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:27.670
So that people can do work offline

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:28.570
when they're not connected.

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:30.700
Is an example of the kinds of things

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.570
that need to be done to enable

00:20:32.570 --> 00:20:36.440
that kind of ability to use these tools.

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:38.470
We also been working with
the Indonesian government

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:40.550
on like data availability.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:43.510
We've been working with making more

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:46.200
Chromebooks available in
California during COVID.

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:49.720
So we're working on like
the overall set of tooling

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:54.720
so that the basic sets of tools
are more broadly available.

00:20:55.010 --> 00:20:58.450
And I think that's really
an important aspect

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:01.923
of making education work for everybody.

00:21:03.440 --> 00:21:04.273
- Yeah.

00:21:04.273 --> 00:21:05.270
Absolutely.

00:21:05.270 --> 00:21:06.617
Do you think there's

00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:11.833
things that when we
think about in the tools,

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:16.160
there's something that things,

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:18.590
as you're thinking about new
tools that you're creating.

00:21:18.590 --> 00:21:19.730
I know there are concerns

00:21:19.730 --> 00:21:22.990
as we get more and more
machine learning and AI.

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:26.100
That are we training them the right ways?

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:29.510
Are we just replicating
our existing biases

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:31.140
in these new forms.

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:33.320
There are ways we can think about

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:36.901
making sure we're not doing that.

00:21:36.901 --> 00:21:39.057
- You know, that's a
really important question

00:21:39.057 --> 00:21:40.731
and we work pretty...

00:21:40.731 --> 00:21:42.010
There's a lot of work going on

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:43.640
both in a research sense

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:46.350
